<task id="020" project="visual-host-create-button-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Build shared WizardFollowOns module + net-new AddTodoFollowOnStep</title>
    <phase>D: WizardFollowOns Consolidation</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>4</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>015</dependencies>
    <blocks>021,022,023,024</blocks>
    <tags>shared-lib, consolidation, fluent-ui</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>New shared module that four existing wizards will consume</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Foundation of a cross-cutting consolidation; the config-driven contract must fit 4 divergent wizard card sets</model-tier-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Create a single config-driven WizardFollowOns module (FollowOnGrid + reusable follow-on steps, incl. the net-new AddTodoFollowOnStep) that will replace the four duplicated Next-Steps implementations. Export from the shared-lib root.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE shared-UI developer. React 18 + Fluent v9. Follow ADR-012 + §11 (one excellent component, not forks).</role>
  <goal>components/WizardFollowOns/ with FollowOnGrid (config-driven card grid → addDynamicStep, zero-selection = early finish), followOnTypes (FollowOnCardConfig + id/label/canonical-order maps), and reusable steps SendEmailFollowOnStep, AddTodoFollowOnStep (net-new, calls todoService.createTodo), AssignWorkFollowOnStep, CreateEventFollowOnStep, DraftSummaryFollowOnStep; exported from src/index.ts.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Today NextSteps/SendEmail are duplicated across CreateRecordWizard, CreateWorkAssignmentWizard, CreateMatterWizard, SummarizeFilesWizard (only EmailStep is shared). design §5.9. The grid must be config-driven so each wizard's card set is FollowOnCardConfig[], not a fork. AddTodoFollowOnStep seeds the To Do's regarding to the created child via applyResolverFields.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WizardFollowOns/ (new)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/FollowOnSteps.tsx (source of truth to generalize)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/steps/
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailStep/
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateTodoWizard/todoService.ts
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      projects/visual-host-create-button-r1/design.md
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/FollowOnSteps.tsx
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/NextStepsSelectionStep.tsx
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateTodoWizard/todoService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailStep/SendEmailStep.tsx
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Wizard/wizardShellTypes.ts
      .claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step>Design FollowOnCardConfig { id, label, icon, description, renderStep } + FOLLOW_ON_ID_MAP / LABEL_MAP / CANONICAL_ORDER in followOnTypes.ts.</step>
    <step>Build FollowOnGrid consuming cards + the shell's addDynamicStep/removeDynamicStep; zero selection = early finish.</step>
    <step>Move/generalize the reusable steps into steps/: SendEmailFollowOnStep (wraps shared EmailStep), AssignWorkFollowOnStep, CreateEventFollowOnStep, DraftSummaryFollowOnStep.</step>
    <step>Build net-new AddTodoFollowOnStep: collect To Do fields, call todoService.createTodo, seed regarding to the created child via applyResolverFields.</step>
    <step>Export the module from src/index.ts. Do NOT yet delete the old copies (that happens in 021-024).</step>
    <step>Add unit tests for grid selection → dynamic step + AddTodoFollowOnStep create path.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>Read, Grep, Edit, Write, Skill(code-review)</tools>
  <outputs>components/WizardFollowOns/ (FollowOnGrid, followOnTypes, steps/*, index.ts); root export.</outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>A wizard can render an arbitrary FollowOnCardConfig[]; selecting a card adds its dynamic step; zero selection = early finish.</criterion>
    <criterion>AddTodoFollowOnStep creates a To Do regarding the child via applyResolverFields.</criterion>
    <criterion>Shared lib builds; tests pass; module exported from root.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
